ionale": "The polling average and fundamentals point to a narrow race, but the freshest and highest-quality surveys plus all three prediction markets favor Acton by a consistent margin, justifying a small Democratic edge over the state's Republican lean. Ramaswamy's fundraising advantage keeps this well short of Likely.", "watch": "Ramaswamy's ad spending from his large war chest, and whether economic concerns keep breaking Acton's way, could move the race either direction.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike DeWine (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Ohio's open governor's race pits Democrat Amy Acton against Republican Vivek Ramaswamy, with term-limited Mike DeWine leaving the seat vacant. Most expert raters call it a tossup, though the Silver Bulletin rates it a Democratic lean. Recent polling has broken toward Acton: a late-September Marist survey showed her up six among registered voters, and a Bowling Green/YouGov likely-voter poll had her ahead by three, consistent with averages placing her up roughly four to six points. Prediction markets on Kalshi, Polymarket, and PredictIt all price her near 60 percent.\n\nThe race remains genuinely competitive. Ohio's partisan lean favors Republicans, Ramaswamy has raised and banked far more money than Acton, and GOP advertising attacking her record is already on air. A narrow Democratic edge with substantial uncertainty is the most defensible read, with turnout and the economic environment likely to decide the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.545, "margin": 0.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5929, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5919, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6166, "margin": 1.3}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5684, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.592, "margin": 1.4}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_